+## Cancellation
+
+Pass an `AbortSignal` to cancel tasks that have not started yet. Unlike `clearQueue()`, the cancelled tasks reject with the signal's `reason`, so awaiting them tells you what was skipped:
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 5, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const urls = getUrls(); // Assume this returns a large list of URLs
+
+// Give up on whatever has not started after 10 seconds
+setTimeout(() => {
+	controller.abort(new Error('Timed out'));
+}, 10_000);
+
+const results = await Promise.allSettled(urls.map(url => limit(() => fetch(url))));
+
+const completed = results.filter(result => result.status === 'fulfilled');
+console.log(`Fetched ${completed.length} of ${urls.length} URLs`);
+```
+
+Already running tasks are not cancelled. To also abort the work itself, forward the signal to it, for example `fetch(url, {signal: controller.signal})`.
+
 ## Dynamic concurrency

 Adjust concurrency at runtime, for example, in response to rate limiting:
