+### limit(options, fn, ...args)
+
+Same as `limit(fn, ...args)`, but lets you cancel this specific task while it's still queued.
+
+#### options
+
+Type: `object`
+
+##### signal
+
+Type: [`AbortSignal`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal)
+
+If the signal is aborted while the task is still queued (i.e. it has not started running yet), the returned promise rejects with the signal's abort reason and the task is removed from the queue.
+
+Note: This has no effect once the task has started running.
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const limit = pLimit(1);
+const controller = new AbortController();
+
+const runningPromise = limit(() => doSomething());
+const queuedPromise = limit({signal: controller.signal}, () => doSomethingElse());
+
+controller.abort();
+
+await runningPromise; // Resolves normally.
+await queuedPromise; // Rejects with the abort reason, `doSomethingElse` never runs.
+```
+
 ### limit.map(iterable, mapperFunction)

 Process an iterable of inputs with limited concurrency.
