+## Cancel queued tasks with an `AbortSignal`
+
+Pass a `signal` to reject the tasks that are still queued when the signal is aborted. Tasks that already started keep running, so use `Promise.allSettled` if you want to wait for the outcome of every task:
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 5, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const urls = getUrls(); // Assume this returns a large list of URLs
+
+// Give up on whatever has not started after 10 seconds
+setTimeout(() => {
+	controller.abort(new Error('Took too long'));
+}, 10_000);
+
+const results = await Promise.allSettled(urls.map(url => limit(() => fetch(url))));
+```
