+## Cancellation with `AbortSignal`
+
+Pass a `signal` to cancel queued tasks. Pass the same signal to the work itself to also stop what is already running:
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 5, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const urls = getUrls(); // Assume this returns a large list of URLs
+
+const promises = urls.map(url => limit(async () => {
+	const response = await fetch(url, {signal: controller.signal});
+	return response.json();
+}));
+
+// Cancel everything that has not finished, for example when the user navigates away
+setTimeout(() => {
+	controller.abort();
+}, 5000);
+
+const results = await Promise.allSettled(promises);
+```
+
+Queued tasks reject with the abort reason, so use `Promise.allSettled` (or catch the rejection) to inspect partial results.
+
 ## Dynamic concurrency

 Adjust concurrency at runtime, for example, in response to rate limiting:
